You need to use dd or rawrite (windows) to write the images to a floppy. 
Unless things have changed, you need a boot floppy image and a RAM disk 
image. 
The images are usually available in a directory on the 1st disk in the set 
labled 'images'.

If you are till stuck, let me know and I will grab an ISO and look for the 
images that you need. 

Also, if you search the archives there is information on booting miata 
from CDROM directly. I have never personally been able to get this to work 
although I didn't apply any of the latest round of info as I was already 
up an running. That would eliminate the floppy image problem.

James



