I've seen things like this before; it's usually the developer's 
way of obtaining a bitwise IEEE754 representation of positive 
infinity (otherwise represented as macro HUGE_VAL or INFINITY 
from math.h).  I don't know what the developer was trying to do 
here, though.

The code behaves the same way on my system (ev56) as it does on 
yours, and I'm pretty sure my compiler is solid (gcc-3.2 release 
with a few bugfix patches).  So I would expect you're getting 
the correct output.

-- 
