> I was able to boot the RH 7.1 iso on my Miata
> so I would try the 7.2 like this:
> Restart the Miata - should get an SRM prompt
> (If not use AlphaBIOS to set OS=Unix)
> at the SRM prompt type
> 
> >>>show dev
> 
> Depending on hardware you should see devices
> labelled the DEC way - I have:
> 
> dva0 - the floppy
> dkc600 - a SCSI hard disk
> dka0 - the ISA CDROM
> 
> put the iso CD in the drive and try:
> 
> >>>boot dka0
> 
> The generic kernel "should" start up and
> from there its a standard RH install,
> after installing I rebuilt the kernel
> with CONFIG_ALPHA_MIATA defined,
