I use the "cdrecord" command to burn ISOs to a disc.  I use
the -v switch to get more verbosity.  At one time, I had to
add "fs=4000k" to side-step a disagreement on whether 4M was
4000K or 4096K, but an update to the cdrecord.conf file has
apparently fixed that.  The only other argument is the name
of the ISO file.

Good luck.

