Just a thought, just in case you haven't already covered it.  On my
UP2000s, the CDROM is referred to as DQA0.  DKA0 is where I put my boot
disk, and was empty when I first started the install.  Usually, the
CDROM drive is at SCSI ID 4, so it may also be accessible as DKA400.
If this is the same setup on your system, you should make sure that you
are actually booting from the CDROM drive, and not an empty SCSI disk.
You can do a show device to see for sure.

eyc




