Yes. All the (recoverable) oops'es occured within the stxncpy routine. There is no oops anymore if the two patches for stxncpy.S and ev6-stxncpy.S are removed from patch-2.4.20-rc1 (or any other 2.4.20 patch since pre9). I never tried to compile in the de4x5 driver.

The oops during X startup may be due to upgrading to XFree86-4.2.0-72. Each time I start X on my PC164 dmesg reports a machine check

CIA machine check: vector=0x670 pc=0x120073ed4 code=0x98
