>From: "G.L. Grobe" <gary@grobe.net>
>Subject: Re: needing image
>Date: Thu, 5 Dec 2002 00:48:43 -0600
>
>Sorry to spam the list, but I need to clarify that last ...
>
>... meaning ... when I view the CD, should I just see the file name of the
>ISO copied onto it or should I actually see a directory structure layout of
>the contents? Because right now all I have is a single file name as follows
>that's just under 659 when viewing the cd contents.
>
>RedHat-7.2-alpha-20020627-disk1.iso

Well, there is your problem...your CD writer software did not burn the
image onto the CD, but copied the image file onto the CD as a CDFS.
You will need to set the option on your CD burner software or find a
writer app that will actually burn the image onto the CD.  When it's
properly done, you should be able to see a directory struture
containing:

autorun  COPYING  images   README           RedHat         RPM-GPG-KEY
boot     etc      kernels  README-Alpha-HW  RELEASE-NOTES  TRANS.TBL

Also on the CD is a boot block that you will not see with a standard
directory listing.

eyc




