For the interested: xine ESD sound is broken on alpha because src/libmad/layer3.c does not compile properly with optimization level -O2 or higher. I could not identify the reason; it might be a bug in the gcc's shipped with RH7.1 and RH7.2. My patch just sets the optimization level to -O1 for all sources in src/libmad.

	Oliver

> In my experience the latest xine from http://cambuca.ldhs.cetuc.puc-rio.br/xine/ still has an issue > with esd sound. This patch is a workaround

--- xine-lib.spec~	Wed Sep  4 08:31:33 2002
+++ xine-lib.spec	Thu Dec  5 12:22:45 2002
@@ -178,6 +178,7 @@
 	    --localstatedir=%{_localstatedir} \
 	    --sharedstatedir=%{_sharedstatedir} --mandir=%{_mandir} \
 	    --infodir=%{_infodir} $BUILD_ARGS
+perl -pi -e "s,-O3,-O1,g" src/libmad/Makefile*
 make
 
 %install
-




