** My previous message had the patch inline and is being held for
** approval.  Here is a repeat of the message with a pointer to
** the patch.

> > Instead, I quickly hacked on the mplayer source and compiled it with the
> > Compaq compiler ccc.  I also move the mpeg alpha optimizations from
> > mplayerxp to the mplayer source.
> >
> > If you want a patch, I can post it.
>
> Yes, that would be great!!

Here it is.  Again, it was a quick hack to compile it under ccc.  I'm
sure it could be improved.  I added the alpha optimizations to libmpeg2
from mplayerxp.

1) Download and untar MPlayer-0.90pre10
2) cd MPlayer-0.90pre10
3) mkdir asm
4) ln -s /usr/include/asm/types.h asm/byteorder.h
        (this is a hack to make ccc happy with linux/cdrom.h)
5) patch -p1 < MPlayer-0.90pre10-alpha.patch
6) CFLAGS="-O4 -fast -inline speed -arch host -tune host" ./configure --cc=ccc -
-disable-gcc-checking --with-extraincdir=".:.."
7) make
        (the make depend stage will bomb)
8) make
        (the second make will build mplayer)

Patch is at http://www.isi.edu/~lindell/alpha/MPlayer-0.90pre10-alpha.patch

Improvements on the patch or build process gladly accepted.

Bob




