Dear Gary, & list

I had similar problems with my PWS500a.  My opinion is that these
machines have a flaky IDE/ATAPI setup.  I could not get my RH 7.1 cds to
install to save my life, although the Compaq "jumpstart" and firmware
disks loaded and did their thing just fine.  

I solved the problem by getting a Sony IDE CDrom drive.  That one didn't
always work either and i found a 68-pin scsi IBM cdrom at
pc-surplusonline.com.

If it is gonna work, it will boot with a 

boot dkaXXX -fl ""
or 
boot dkaXXX -fl 0

The alternative is to boot from floppies.  When i got my machine i had
to run it 24 hours straight before it would read the boot sector of a
floppy.  Actually, warming up the chipset for a day or so might5 improve
your luck installing from the Toshiba CDrom.

good luck

jn


