> When I open the tray and type 'boot dka0' I get ...
>    dka0.0.0.4.0 has no media present or is disabled via the RUN/STOP switch
> 
> If I close the tray and type 'boot dka0' I get ...
>    failed to open dka0.0.0.4.0
> 
> If I open the tray, type the command, then close the tray I get the 'not
> present' error displayed and once it's closed it prints the 'failed to open'
> msg.
> 

Well that is not good - it is not reading the CD at all.
I have only one further suggestion:
Maybe your CD reader cannot read the kind of CD recordable
that you are using. Have you tried reading a "real" CD
Any that was manufactured - even one of those AOL CD's that
come in the mail will do. If it can read it SRM will say
"invalid boot block" or some such - if not you could try cleaning
the optics but it is not hopeful. If it does read it then
it may be an older CD reader that is having trouble with the
lower contrast on the new CD recordable disks. Good luck,

Stephen Lewis




