First, I apologized for the email format - they make us use Lotus Notes :-/

I have 3 questions - I tried to search the archives but all of the searches
gave 0 findings.  Sorry, I know these questions have been asked b4.

I have a PWS600au (miata) that I am trying to install 7.2 on.  I downloaded
the 7.2 iso's right after it was released (a long time ago).  I remember
seeing something on the list about the original iso's being bad.  Was this
correct?  Do I need to download new iso's?

Booting from the first cd works great (original ide cdrom), but when it
starts anaconda and the graphical installer, it is just a garbled mess on
the screen.  The video card is a Compaq Powerstorm350.  I've never used
this card before, so I know nothing about it.  This problem appears to be
poor framebuffer support for it.  But will I have future problems with X
support as well?

To summarize, my questions are:
1.  Should I get new iso's?
2.  Is the Powerstorm 350 supported well by Xfree?
3.  Any idea on why the graphical installer is garbled? (probably related
to question 2)

Thx.
