To the list:

A couple months ago, I posted a bit about my probelms with my pws500a/u
losing it and going black-screen and unresponsive at the point where the
login screen is supposed to come up.  I got no replies at all on that
one, but later tried starting in text mode and issuing the startx
command.  The return was that the Xserver was not where it the OS was
looking for it.  I quit for a while and worked on my Tru64 installation.

This week i did a clean, standard workstation reinstallation of RH 7.2
and selected text login as default when offered the choice.  I did a
startx and got about 1/2 of the Genome desktop, enough for my own uses. 
Then I switched to KDE and got almost all of it.  I have been using it
since then.

Many thanks to Mike Harris and the others for the 7.2 distro.  I can
tell right off it is an improvement over 7.1.  It even seems to load
faster.  Good work, guys.

My own thought is that rather than keeping up with the (PC) Joneses on
numbered distributions, maybe we should try for incremental upgrades to
the kernel, libraries, and key applications.

I am posting this from my PC as the list software doesn't recognize me
when I am using the Alpha. 

my 2 cents

jn 





