The 9000 PCI by Powercolor is out.  I got one at our local Fry's Electronics     
(Oregon) about three weeks ago.  It was $119 dollars.  SRM 5.8-1 in a       
LX initializes it fine.  For X support, you'll need to go to XFree CVS      
and possibly the DRI CVS.  I'm using the DRI CVS on top of 4.2.             
I have not had any 2D problems.  The DRI CVS has some 3D hardware support,
but it is not stable.  It locks the box.  From the messages I have seen
on the DRI-devel list, the lockups happen on x86 too.  The unaccelerated
3D (software only) drivers work ok.  So it seems to be a general driver issue.
If you are looking at it for fast hardware 3D, you might want to wait a bit
until the driver stablizes before committing to getting a card.

Alan




