Yup, that's a reasonable card.

> Most of our miata workstations have the TGA2 2MB cards in them.  Are they
> supported?  I'm assuming not.  We have about 45 of these miata's not being
> used.  I was going to see about getting them donated to the local
> university.  They want to set up a  cluster with them, so if they're
> headless that might work just fine.

TGA2 *is* supported under XFree86 4.1.0 as found in RH 7.2.

> This 600au I set up yesterday is the first one I've set up that has the
> Bcache module.  I'm impressed with the improvement.  Anyone know how I can
> get more of these Bcache modules?  I've asked before but nobody responded.
> Not even from the Island... ;-)

Unfortunately, they were expensive. If you really go for them, try to get
the 4MB module (AOT the 2MB one); there is a noticeable difference...

One weird side effect of not having the Bcache module is that graphics
intensive stuff actually goes a bit faster (ie CPU/memory to PCI bus
traffic), because the cache actually gets in the way a bit when it's
there...

