On Tue, Dec 10, 2002 at 02:42:11PM -0600, G.L. Grobe wrote:
> 
> Video:
> Seems the Radeon 8500 is going to be a good choice from what I'm hearing.
> I'd just like to view something really nice once I have enough of a card to
> run Gnome or KDE.

8500, AFAIK, does NOT come in a PCI version. Go with 7000 or, better,
a 7500; at the moment, the support for the 9000 PCI is not there WRT
3D, but 2D is reported to work.

> CD-Rom:
> What do ya'll suggest for a CD-Rom? It currently has a Toshiba XM-57 (from
> the 'show dev'). Is there any way for this box to accept USB devices? I'd
> sure like to just plug in my external Yamaha CD-RW.

The builtin USB is not recommended; your best option for USB is to
install an add-in card. But I don't know if any of the USB 2.0 cards
have been checked out on Al[pha yet (anyone?).

Most PWSes had a Toshiba IDE CDROM when new. I'd stick with name brand
ones for replacements, like Sony or TDK or Pioneer or Plextor. Don't
go with a DVD as a replacement, as some are incompatible with the SRM
console expectations (usually block-size related).

> And on a curious note, can the processor be ugraded to
> something higher on this box? Might help in knowing what I need ... can buy
> for spare parts.

CPUs were clocked to 600 in the PWS; I don't know what would be
involved in upgrading a 433 or 500 to 600, but most likley not just
jumpers/crystal. Oh, I think the Bcache modules were different as well.

> I'd like to up the 256Mb of RAM it has once I find out what
> sort of RAM it takes.

That info has been posted before; search the archives (I just don't
remember off-hand)...

