> 
> Most of our miata workstations have the TGA2 2MB cards in 
> them.  Are they
> supported?  

Yes, they are. But, they aren't too interesting. You will only get 8 bit color out of them.

"Powerstorm" was a "marketing name" applied to a bunch of totally unrelated cards.

IIRC, 

Supported - PowerStorm 3D30 & 4D20 (TGA2; thanks to work Jay did a while back).
            PowerStorm 4D10 - DEC version of a Permedia 2 card.

Unsupported- PowerStorm 4D40T/50T/51T/60T - (Intergraph "Realizm I" based cards)
             PowerStorm 300 & 350 - E&S cards




