The Miatas use standard 83.3Mhz (PC100 or greater works) 168 pin SDRAM. I 
don't know if it has to be ECC unregistered or non-ECC sdram as I only use 
ECC in mine. THe motherboard will support up to 1.5GB of RAM in DIMM 
pairs. The pairs must be the same size (e.g. 2 128MB dimms). etc.

CDROM - I had to replace mine. I have actually used a couple, vanilla, 
ATAPI CDROM drives in it. I don't recall and particular manufacture. 
Sorry.

Video cards - I have used S3 and Permidia 2 most succesfully. I have an 
ATI that I need to update my SRM version in order to use it. It is an 
ALL-IN-WONDER 128 Pro.

$.02

James
