Today we use Applixware Mail for the following reasons:

1. Both global and local addressbooks.
   Eg it's enterprise, not single user
2. Incomming filetype detection and implicicit format conversion on reading
   attachments.
   Eg it has a capability to launch applications depending on the incomming
   attachemnt.
3. Global recipient list that auto converts formats on outgoing mail.
   Eg. useres donnot have to bother with format conversions on outgoing
   mail. It's fully automatic depending on the recipeint profile
   setup in a global list. So it works for all users, eg it's enterprise,
   not single user.

It allso have som flaws: 1. poor, not up-to-date attachmentment recognition, 2. 
cannot work with attachements containg spaces in filenames, 3. problems with 
international characters in the subject line and a couple more.

I have searched other mailers in Linux for corresponding features and found 
none.

Any ideas?

Hilsen
