As you may have noticed, earlier this week I installed RH7.2 on a PWS600au.
I have 3 scsi drives.  Everything has been working well.

During the installation, I setup 2 of the disks in Software Raid0.  I was
not concerned with redundancy - only make the 2 drives look like 1 and I'm
formatting /dev/md0 as ext3.  However, I forgot to add swap at the
beginning of each drive during the installation.  So now I'm
repartitioning.

Questions
1.  When editing the BSD label using fdisk, type fd (linux software raid)
is not an option.  How was DiskDruid able to do this then?  How do I do it
now?

2.  Is there a way to use DiskDruid separate from the installer?  That gui
was very nice and idiot proof.

3.  Is there a better/easier way to make the two disks look like one?  I'm
accustomed to using ADVFS which I really like.  Too bak HP is not opening
that up like JFS and XFS.  Can ext3 span multiple drives?
