Well, yes and no.   Sort of.  You can always run "update" from your
installation media and this will give you DiskDruid as well if you so
desire.  You do not really have to update anything.

DiskDruid  has its own opinions where to put things, often quite
unexpect ones, so I am not so sure if it is such "idiot proof" as
it may appear in the first moment.

