>    internal ext2 data structures are different in size.

Linux file system go to a great length to make sure that disks are
data compatible between different architectures.   Not that this
is exercised very often so maybe some bugs are lurking there but
in principle this should be fine.  In particular ext2/ext3 are
little-endian regardless of a processor.

   Michal




