chu@tes-mail.jpl.nasa.gov (Eugene Chu) writes:

> I have a question regarding disklabels on Linux/Alpha.  When I use
> fdisk, I am given the ability to create either a DOS label or a DOS
> and BSD label.  Which one do I really need?

If you want to boot via SRM console from that disk, you need BSD labels.
If you want to boot via ARC console from that disk, you need DOS labels.
If you don't want to boot from that disk at all, you can use whatever
you like.

-- 
	Falk




