On Tue, 2002-12-10 at 05:11, G.L. Grobe wrote:
> RH 7.2 reported a successful install, so once the machine rebooted, I've
> tried several combinations of 'boot dkc0 -fl 0' and keep getting output
> similiar to the following ...
> 

IIRC I had a similar problem when I installed RH 7.1 on a Miata about a
year ago. My inability to get the Miata to boot after an, apparently,
successfull install, was due to an unsuccessfull installation of the
secondary bootstrap loader (aboot).

The aboot installer failed because there was overlap between the
partition where aboot was supposed to be installed and another
partition. With SunOS, BSD and Digital UNIX you have a "whole disk"
partition that spans the entire disk which will clearly collide with all
other partitions. Thus, the aboot installer (swriteboot, I think) has an
option that tells it to ignore an overlap with a specified partition. 

I don't recall whether the RH installer failed to use this option or I
had a "non-standard" overlap, but both the "ignore overlap" option and
removing the "whole disk" partition solved my problem.

Check your partition table. If you don't have any overlap, I'm afraid
you have a different problem :( Just thought I would share my experience
though.

/magnus

