I'm using apt to distribute updates to about a half-dozen Alphas here. 
It works very well. There is some good information and some useful 
scripts for setting up an apt repository at http://freshrpms.net/apt/ 
which got me going in an afternoon.

I cannot recommend this approach highly enough if you're trying to keep 
groups of machines up to date. I used to use autorpm, but it just needed 
too much manual intervention. Apt handles everything beautifully.




