On Monday 16 December 2002 11:14 am, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
> Sorry guys, but I haven't had my "aha!" moment on this yet:
>
> What is the difference between DRI in Xfree and drm-kernel? 
> Are they the same thing?
>
> Ted

DRM ("Direct Rendering Modules") is the kernel-space portion of 
DRI; it normally comes either from the kernel source tree, or 
from XFree86.  There's also a user-space portion of DRI that 
usually comes with XFree86.

-- 
Kelledin
