On Mon, 16 Dec 2002, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:

> Sorry guys, but I haven't had my "aha!" moment on this yet:
>
> What is the difference between DRI in Xfree and drm-kernel?  Are they
> the same thing?

not quite, but they're related.

I _think_ that dri is direct rendering interface, whereas drm is direct
rendering manager.

dri provides the hooks for XFree to use direct rendering, where drm
provides the hardware interface.

But what do I know?

--
-- John E. Jasen (jjasen1@umbc.edu)
