On Monday 16 December 2002 12:14 pm, Ted Goodridge wrote:
> So, with kernel 2.4.20, which does not come with drm-kernel
> for xfree 4.2 what does it use?  I compiled 4.2 from source. 
> Does it come with the drm-kernel for 4.2?  If so, how do I
> make sure it gets loaded?

Are you sure 2.4.20 doesn't contain the proper driver?  I seem to 
remember getting 2.4.18's DRM to work just fine with a Matrox 
G450 in XFree86-4.2.0.  The kernel option is probably just 
mislabeled a bit.

If you feel you need to use the DRM included with XFree86, it's 
in the programs/Xserver/hw/xfree86/os-support/linux/drm/kernel 
subdirectory of the XFree86 source tree.  It doesn't get 
compiled by default when you run "make World" on XFree86--you 
generally have to go into that directory and compile it 
manually.  It's been ages since I did that, but fortunately 
there seems to be a README.drm in there.

-- 
Kelledin
