On Mon, Dec 16, 2002 at 11:06:18AM -0600, Ted Goodridge, Jr wrote:
>
> Where does one get the Alpha string function patches and regdef.h?
> Stupid question, but I can't remember.  How do you apply a patch to a
> source tree?

The kernel sources and patches are found at:

	www.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel

In particular, the 2.4.21-pre1 patches are found at:

	www.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v2.4/testing/patch-2.4.21-pre1.bz2

Unpack them via:

	bunzip2 patch-2.4.21-pre1.bz2

Apply them via:

	cd /usr/src/linux-2.4.20	# previous source tree
	cat ~/patch-2.4.21-pre1 | patch -p1 -E >& ../log.2.4.21-pre1

That will give you ALL the patches; if you just want to apply the string
ones, you'll have to edit the patch file to extract arch/alpha/lib stuff
and include/asm-alpha/regdef.h.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

