On Mon, Dec 16, 2002 at 04:38:45PM -0500, Bruce Embrey wrote:
>
> I ran into a problem with my video card. I have a AS500au with a
> Radeon 32MB SDRAM PCI card. SRM recognizes it and 7.2 loads up but
> when it switches from text to graphics mode the screen blinks
> momentarily with multi-color blocks and then it comes up in X. If I
> open a terminial session in X text is displayed correctly but if I
> Ctrl-F1 the screen has hashed blocks were text should be. I have
> tried different resolutions and depths without success.

I'm assuming you mean a PWS 500au (aka MIATA), right?

Is the Radeon in one of the 2 64-bit PCI slots? It should be; if the
console complains about it when you put it in there, then do:

	>>> set pci_device_override -1

and try again (ie you may need to keep it in one of the 32-bit slots
to do this at the console level).

Good luck.

 --Jay++

