On Wed, Dec 18, 2002 at 02:33:51PM -0500, Bruce Embrey wrote:
> 
> I have a AlphaServer 800 5/400 that has 2 Qlogic 1020 and 2 DAC960.
> When I boot to the SRM prompt I can see my RAID sets as well as my tape,
> and cdrom. When booting the RedHat 7.2 Disk1 it shows it is loading the
> qlogic driver and the DAC960 driver but when I get to the partitioning
> screen it says I have no drives to install on.

IIRC DAC960 is supported by Linux if it has a firmware version 2.73 or
higher. Some controller models are upgradable and some not.  Search in
archives.  http://www.dandelion.com/Linux/ should have some information
but Leonard Zubkoff, who wrote that driver, unfortunately died in
a helicopter crash.

Qlogic 1020 should be ok although there were some "interesting points"
with this controller too.  People who are actually using it should
know better about possible quirks.

  Michal




