I was able to get a 3 channel DAC960 running (fw =
2.73) on a AS1200.  The process that I used for
installing RH 7.2, was to install onto a temp disk
that was NOT connected to the DAC.  Once installed I
recompiled the kernel and turned on the DAC960
support, booted to the new kernel and was able to see
the controller and the drives that I had configured on
each of the channels.  Once you have gotten to this
step, then you can bring the drives online in the O/S
and move the data to them at your will.  Currently I
have everything but /boot on the raid disks--works
great with ext3 fs.
