On Thu, Dec 19, 2002 at 11:14:20AM +0100, Helge Kreutzmann wrote:
> 
> *) The build dies with some missing symbols:
> depmod: *** Unresolved symbols in
> /scratch/build/src/linux/debian/tmp-image/lib/modules/2.4.21-pre1/kernel/drivers/media/video/tda7432.o
> depmod:         __fixdfsi
> depmod:         __floatsidf
> depmod:         __divdf3
> depmod:         __muldf3
> depmod:         __subdf3
> 
> 
>    tda7432 is build for bttv. 

I do not know what is a fix but this looks like a bug in sources.  These
are symbols from a floating point support library and floating point
cannot be used in a kernel.  It means that operations which caused these
to appear should be provided inside kernel sources.  Quite possible that
nobody did that so far in a case of 'tda7432' and Alpha.  Likely that is
a reason why this kernel configuration option was not selectable.
Checking how x86 is dealing with the issue may give you some ideas.

  Michal




