On Mon, Dec 16, 2002 at 09:41:19AM -0500, Jay Estabrook wrote:
> On Sun, Dec 15, 2002 at 10:12:57AM -0800, Robert M. Riches Jr. wrote:
> > 
> > Will the Radeon 7500 work with UP-2000 SRM version A5.8-81, or
> > does it require a mythical version 5.9 that will apparently never
> > see the light of day?
> 
> I suspect that that UP2000's SRM has BIOS Emulator 2.x or some such,
> IIRC, and not 3.x. That may be the determining factor in whether the
> 7500 works or not, as the jump from BIOSem 2.x to 3.x added support
> for many of the more recent cards (through generic improvements).
> 
> I just tried a PC164 with BIOSem 1.15 (SRM 5.5) and it black-screened.
> 
> I'll try to find an older version of DS10 console with BIOSem 2.x, and
> see if it works or not...

OK, I found a whole set of older SRM update disks, and finally had the
time today to give this a shot...

Into a DS10 I FLASHed SRM V5.5-1, dated June 29, 1999, and it worked
fine with a proto PCI 7500 I have. The BIOSem in v5.5-1 was noted as
V1.15a, which I assume is older than that in your UP2000. SRM V5.9 on
DS10 has BIOSem X2.02.

I assume what your UP2000 has is X2.01, which is in V5.7 and V5.8.

Note that with some cards, one doesn't see the BIOS and BIOSem banners
at the start (my proto 7500 does not), but with other cards it does,
such as Millenniums, for example, so you may have to find a card that
DOES show the info to make sure...

Also, I just tried the proto 7500 in a UP1100 proto I have, which has
an SRM console A5.9-1 dated 28 March 2001, and it WORKED FINE there as
well. The BIOSem in the UP1100 identifies itself as X2.02.

I'm afraid I can't get any closer to your configuration than that, but
I would be EXTREMELY surprised if the retail version of the PCI 7500
did not work in your box.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

