list archives and find like 12000 people asking this very 
question per week.

I'll add one more answer though..

kernel-headers is NOT for compiling kernel modules.  
kernel-source is.

kernel-headers is for glibc and nothing else, and it does not get 
updated ever.  It is the kernel headers that are used to compile 
glibc with.  It is not for any other purpose.

Sorry for being blunt, but I've seen this question at least 20 
times in 2 days, and it gets boring.

No offense.


-- 
Mike A. Harris     ftp://people.redhat.com/mharris
OS Systems Engineer - XFree86 maintainer - Red Hat




