I just ran into a problem that appears to be due to a missing RPM
in the updates area,

    ftp://alpha.crl.dec.com/pub/linux/redhat/7.2-alpha/updates

There's a clump of php*-4.1.2-7.2.6 RPMs that would update a
system from the version 4.1.2-6 that came with the boxed CDs
purchased around July.  However, there is no updated php-dbg RPM.
So, the old php-dbg requires the old php-4.1.2-6 be kept around,
which prevents the whole clump from installing.  My guess is the
new php-dbg is simply missing.

Being as this looked like a bug at some level, I filed it as #33
at http://alpha.crl.dec.com/bugzilla.

Thanks.

Robert Riches
