> > answer?  I would likely use SRM anyway (it is available for
> > LX) unless you have an Adaptec SCSI controller. :-)
>
> Yep, I have Adaptec 2940UW ...

Agreed, SRM is the way to go.  AlphaBIOS is pretty useless unless 
you want to saddle your Alpha box with an obsolete piece of junk 
like (*gasp*) Windows NT 4.

SRM v5.8 for PC164LX recognizes the Adaptec 2940UW without 
problems.  The thing apparently has no problem booting off an 
18GB SCSI drive here...

